[groq-gpt-oss] evals/prompts/lib/skill-p:
Below is a quick-fire “what-went-wrong + how-to-fix it” guide that focuses on the two things you called out – `map.setFog()` and the v2-only free-camera API – and then reminds you of the other migration steps that often get missed when moving from **Mapbox GL JS v2** to **MapLibre GL JS** (v6 at the time of writing).

---

## 1. The short answer: you didn’t do anything *wrong* – the APIs you were using simply **don’t exist in MapLibre**.

| Mapbox GL JS v2 feature | MapLibre equivalent (or “no direct equivalent”) |
|--------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| `map.setFog({...})`      | **`map.setSky({...})`** – uses the `sky` layer in the style spec. |
| `map.getFreeCameraOptions()` / `map.setFreeCameraOptions()` (FreeCameraOptions) | **No FreeCameraOptions class**. Use the new camera-calculation helpers (`calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation`, `calculateCameraOptionsFromTo`) and then call `jumpTo`, `easeTo`, or `flyTo`. |
| `map.setFog` style property (`fog`) | **`sky`** style property (`sky`) – see the MapLibre Style Spec for the exact fields. |

So the migration isn’t “broken”; you just need to replace those calls with the MapLibre-supported ones.

---

## 2. Fixing `map.setFog()` → `map.setSky()`

### 2.1. What changed?

* **Mapbox**: `fog` lives at the *root* of the style JSON and is manipulated with `map.setFog()`.
* **MapLibre**: The same visual effect lives in a **`sky`** object (still at the root of the style) and is manipulated with `map.setSky()`. The property names are a little different.

### 2.2. Minimal code change

```js
// Mapbox (v2)
map.setFog({
  "color": "#f8f4f0",
  "high-color": "#245b8c",
  "space-color": "#c8d0e0",
  "horizon-blend": 0.3
});
```

```js
// MapLibre (v6+)
map.setSky({
  // sky-color = “space-color” in Mapbox
  "sky-color": "#c8d0e0",

  // horizon-color = “high-color” in Mapbox
  "horizon-color": "#245b8c",

  // fog-color = “color” in Mapbox
  "fog-color": "#f8f4f0",

  // blend factors – MapLibre splits the single `horizon-blend`
  // into three separate controls. Pick the one(s) you need.
  "horizon-fog-blend": 0.3,   // how much fog meets the horizon
  "sky-horizon-blend": 0.3,   // how the sky fades into the horizon
  "fog-ground-blend": 0.3,    // how fog meets the ground (optional)
  "atmosphere-blend": 1.0     // overall strength of the atmosphere
});
```

### 2.3. Style-JSON side-effect

If you are loading a style JSON that already contains a `fog` object, you must **rename it to `sky`** and adjust the field names. The easiest way is:

1. Open the style JSON in **Maputnik** (the MapLibre style editor) or any JSON editor.
2. Find the top-level `"fog"` object and replace it with `"sky"`.
3. Rename the inner keys as shown above.
4. Save and reload the map.

> **Tip:** MapLibre ships a tiny helper CLI (`gl-style-validate`) that will warn you if a style still contains unsupported `fog` keys.

```bash
npx gl-style-validate my-style.json   # will flag unknown properties
```

---

## 3. Re-creating the free-camera API

### 3.1. What you lose

* `map.getFreeCameraOptions()` – returns a `FreeCameraOptions` object (lng/lat/alt, bearing, pitch, roll, etc.).
* `map.setFreeCameraOptions(opts)` – directly sets the camera from that object.

MapLibre never added those methods. Instead it provides **camera-calculation helpers** that return a plain `CameraOptions` object, which you then feed to the standard camera movement methods (`jumpTo`, `easeTo`, `flyTo`).

### 3.2. The new workflow

```js
// 1️⃣  Compute a CameraOptions object from the parameters you would have
//     passed to FreeCameraOptions.
const camOpts = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation({
  lng: -122.42,
  lat: 37.78,
  altitude: 5000          // metres above the ground (or sea level)
}, {
  bearing: 45,            // degrees clockwise from north
  pitch: 60,              // degrees from the horizon
  roll: 0                 // optional, added in v5
});

// 2️⃣  Apply the camera – choose the transition you want.
map.jumpTo(camOpts);               // instant
// or
map.easeTo(camOpts, {duration: 2000}); // smooth
// or
map.flyTo(camOpts, {maxDuration: 5000}); // “fly” animation
```

If you need a **look-at** (camera positioned so that it points from point A to point B), use the older helper:

```js
const camOpts = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromTo(
  {lng: -122.42, lat: 37.78, altitude: 5000}, // from
  {lng: -122.45, lat: 37.80, altitude: 0}     // to (ground target)
);
map.easeTo(camOpts);
```

### 3.3. Mapping the old `FreeCameraOptions` fields

| FreeCameraOptions field | MapLibre equivalent (via helper) |
|------------------------|-----------------------------------|
| `center` (lng/lat)     | first argument of `calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation` |
| `altitude`             | same argument (`altitude`) |
| `bearing`              | same argument (`bearing`) |
| `pitch`                | same argument (`pitch`) |
| `roll` (v5+)           | same argument (`roll`) |
| `zoom`                 | **not part of FreeCameraOptions** – you can add `zoom` to the returned `CameraOptions` manually if you need it. |

---

## 4. Checklist – Did you miss any other migration steps?

| ✅ | Item | Why it matters |
|---|------|----------------|
| 1 | **Uninstall `mapbox-gl` and install `maplibre-gl`** (`npm i maplibre-gl`) | Guarantees you’re pulling the right code. |
| 2 | **Update imports / CDN** – use `import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl'` (or the ES-module CDN) and `import 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css'`. | v6 is ES-module-only; the old UMD bundle is gone. |
| 3 | **Rename the namespace** – replace every `mapboxgl` with `maplibregl`. | Otherwise you’ll get “undefined” errors. |
| 4 | **Remove `mapboxgl.accessToken`** – MapLibre does not read a global token. | Leaving it in does nothing, but it can be confusing. |
| 5 | **Swap the style URL** – `mapbox://styles/...` → a non-Mapbox style (e.g. OpenFreeMap, your own hosted style, or a style you exported from Mapbox Studio and edited). | MapLibre cannot fetch Mapbox-hosted tiles without a token. |
| 6 | **Fix style JSON** – replace any `source` URLs that start with `mapbox://` (tiles, sprites, glyphs) with URLs for your new tile provider. | Otherwise the map will load a blank style or 401 errors. |
| 7 | **Update plugins** – many Mapbox UI plugins work unchanged, but some (e.g. `mapbox-gl-geocoder`) have MapLibre forks (`@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder`). | Using the Mapbox version will throw “cannot find module” or “unknown control”. |
| 8 | **Replace Mapbox REST APIs** (Geocoding, Directions, etc.) with open alternatives (Nominatim, OSRM, OpenRouteService, MapTiler Cloud, etc.). | Those endpoints are proprietary and require a token. |
| 9 | **Replace v2-only methods** – `setFog` → `setSky`; free-camera → `calculateCameraOptions…` + `jumpTo/easeTo/flyTo`. | As covered above. |
|10| **CSS class prefixes** – if you wrote custom CSS targeting `.mapboxgl-ctrl`, rename to `.maplibregl-ctrl`. | Otherwise your custom styling disappears. |
|11| **Test on a clean build** – clear caches, rebuild, and verify the map loads, controls appear, and any custom layers render. | Guarantees you didn’t miss a stray `mapboxgl` reference. |

---

## 5. Full-example migration (minimal app)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre migration demo</title>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script type="module">
  import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';

  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty', // any non-Mapbox style
    center: [-122.42, 37.78],
    zoom: 12,
    pitch: 45,
    bearing: 0
  });

  // ---- Fog → Sky -------------------------------------------------
  map.on('load', () => {
    map.setSky({
      'sky-color': '#c8d0e0',
      'horizon-color': '#245b8c',
      'fog-color': '#f8f4f0',
      'horizon-fog-blend': 0.3,
      'sky-horizon-blend': 0.3,
      'fog-ground-blend': 0.3,
      'atmosphere-blend': 1.0
    });
  });

  // ---- Free-camera replacement ------------------------------------
  // Example: move the camera to a high-altitude viewpoint over the city
  const camOpts = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation(
    {lng: -122.42, lat: 37.78, altitude: 4000},
    {bearing: 30, pitch: 70, roll: 0}
  );

  // Instant jump (or use easeTo/flyTo for animation)
  map.jumpTo(camOpts);
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

*Run the page in a modern browser (ES-module support required). The map should load, show a sky/fog effect, and the camera should be positioned at the altitude you specified.*

